  quiz: [
    { q: ['用 NaOH 滴定弱酸，半等当点的 pH 等于：', 'Titrating a weak acid with NaOH, the pH at half-equivalence equals:'], opts: [['该酸的 pKa', 'the acid’s pKa'], ['7', '7'], ['等当点 pH 的一半', 'half the equivalence pH'], ['14 − pKa', '14 − pKa']], a: 0, why: ['半等当点 [HA] = [A⁻]，Henderson–Hasselbalch 方程给出 pH = pKa。', 'At half-equivalence [HA] = [A⁻], and Henderson–Hasselbalch gives pH = pKa.'], ch: 'acidbase' },
    { q: ['EDTA 滴定 Ca²⁺ 要在 pH 10 左右而不是 pH 4，主要因为：', 'EDTA titrations of Ca²⁺ are run near pH 10 rather than pH 4 mainly because:'], opts: [['低 pH 时 αY⁴⁻ 很小，条件形成常数不够大', 'at low pH αY⁴⁻ is tiny and the conditional constant too small'], ['Ca²⁺ 在 pH 4 会水解', 'Ca²⁺ hydrolyses at pH 4'], ['指示剂在 pH 4 不显色', 'the indicator has no colour at pH 4'], ['EDTA 在酸中分解', 'EDTA decomposes in acid']], a: 0, why: ['K′ = αY⁴⁻ K_f；pH 4 时 αY⁴⁻ 约 10⁻⁸ 量级，K′ 远不够。', 'K′ = αY⁴⁻ K_f; at pH 4 αY⁴⁻ is around 10⁻⁸, far too small.'], ch: 'complexation' },
    { q: ['5 次平行测定的标准偏差是 s，平均值的 95 % 置信区间半宽是：', 'Five replicates have standard deviation s. The half-width of the 95 % confidence interval of the mean is:'], opts: [['2.776 s/√5', '2.776 s/√5'], ['1.96 s', '1.96 s'], ['2.776 s', '2.776 s'], ['s/√5', 's/√5']], a: 0, why: ['自由度 4 的 t = 2.776，乘以平均值的标准误 s/√n。', 't for 4 degrees of freedom is 2.776, times the standard error s/√n.'], ch: 'stats' },
    { q: ['提高色谱分离度最有效的通常是：', 'The most effective way to improve chromatographic resolution is usually:'], opts: [['提高选择性 α', 'raising the selectivity α'], ['把柱子加长一倍', 'doubling the column length'], ['把流速加倍', 'doubling the flow rate'], ['提高检测器灵敏度', 'a more sensitive detector']], a: 0, why: ['R_s 只随 √N 增长，柱长加倍只提高约 41 %；α 稍有变化影响很大。流速偏离最佳值反而降低柱效。', 'R_s grows only as √N, so doubling the length gains about 41 %; small changes in α matter much more. Moving the flow rate away from the optimum lowers efficiency.'], ch: 'separations' },
    { q: ['标准加入法主要用来克服：', 'Standard addition is mainly used to overcome:'], opts: [['基体效应', 'matrix effects'], ['仪器漂移', 'instrument drift'], ['随机误差', 'random error'], ['检出限太高', 'a high detection limit']], a: 0, why: ['标准直接加在样品里，与待测物处于同一基体，信号受同样的影响。', 'Standards are added to the sample itself and experience the same matrix as the analyte.'], ch: 'calibration' },
    { q: ['电喷雾电离和 MALDI 被称为“软电离”，是因为：', 'Electrospray and MALDI are called “soft” ionisation because:'], opts: [['能让大分子完整地成为气相离子', 'they bring large molecules intact into the gas phase as ions'], ['用的能量很低所以灵敏度低', 'they use little energy and so are insensitive'], ['只能电离软物质', 'they ionise only soft matter'], ['不需要真空', 'they need no vacuum']], a: 0, why: ['相比电子轰击，它们几乎不让分子碎裂，所以能测蛋白质和聚合物的分子量。', 'Unlike electron ionisation they barely fragment molecules, so proteins and polymers can be weighed.'], ch: 'instrumental' },
    { q: ['PLS 模型的交叉验证误差随潜变量数先降后升，应选：', 'A PLS model’s cross-validation error first falls then rises with the number of latent variables. Choose:'], opts: [['误差最小（或接近最小）时的潜变量数', 'the number at (or near) the minimum error'], ['最多的潜变量', 'as many as possible'], ['一个潜变量', 'just one'], ['使校准误差最小的数目', 'the number that minimises calibration error']], a: 0, why: ['再多的潜变量只是在拟合噪声；校准误差总随潜变量增加而降低，不能用来选择。', 'More latent variables just fit noise; calibration error always falls as they are added and cannot be used to choose.'], ch: 'chemometrics' },
  ],
